      "title": "Public Services Librarian",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-20\n\nLocation: AVE MARIA\n\nThe Public Service Librarian manages the activities and operations of the Library. This staff member's work involves circulation, reference, online services, bibliographic instruction, course reserves, and interlibrary loan/document delivery.     ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:  Supervises all aspects of Public Services. Establishes policies, standards, and procedures for the department in all areas of public service.   Provides reference and research assistance to patrons. Provides library instruction when called upon by academic faculty. Serves as public services liaison with faculty, soliciting faculty input and coordinating academic initiatives between library and academics. Establishes and maintains access to electronic resources.   Oversees the physical layout of the public area of the library.   Runs and analyzes library usage statistics. Serves as Systems Librarian for the library’s Integrated Library System (WorldShare Management System). Maintains the library’s website. Takes the lead in hiring and training staff. EDUCATION: Bachelor’s degree from four-year college. Master’s degree from an ALA-accredited library program or equivalent . EXPERIENCE:  At least three years spent professionally in an academic environment, either in the Library or at an academic position. Supervisory experience strongly preferred. CERTIFICATION:  Master’s degree from an ALA-Accredited program or equivalent.   PHYSICAL SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Position requires sitting for long periods of time and the visual and manual ability to use a computer keyboard. Requires ordinary ambulatory skills sufficient to visit other locations; or the ability to stand, walk and manipulate (lift, carry, move) weights of up to 40 lbs and the ability to push a fully loaded book cart. Packing and unpacking boxes of books may be required.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205226383124_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor of Latin",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-13\n\nLocation: AVE MARIA\n\nAve Maria University seeks applicants for a part-time adjunct faculty position teaching elementary and intermediate Latin. Qualified candidates will possess a master’s degree or terminal degree in the field. Candidates with teaching experience in higher education are strongly preferred. TO APPLY :   Applicants should register here within the Ave Maria University’s online talent management site and upload their cover letter, curriculum vitae, three references, and a statement relating the University’s Catholic mission as expressed in  Ex Corde Ecclesiae  to their philosophy of teaching addressed to: Dr. Bradley Ritter, Chair and Associate Professor of Classics and Early Christian Literature, at Bradley.Ritter@avemaria.edu, Ave Maria University, 5050 Ave Maria Blvd., Ave Maria, FL 34142.    Review of applications will continue until the position is filled.  Incomplete applications will not be considered. Ave Maria University does not discriminate in employment opportunities, practices, or the terms and conditions of employment based on race, color, sex, national origin, age, disability, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law.",
